# See https://aquasecurity.github.io/trivy/v0.48/docs/configuration/filtering/#trivyignore

# The following CVEs appear in workspace sub-module go.mod files (apps/*, pkg/*) but are
# FALSE POSITIVES. This repo uses Go workspace mode (go.work). When building, Go's Minimum
# Version Selection picks the MAXIMUM version across all workspace modules — so the patched
# versions in the root go.mod (v1.43.0 for otel, v1.80.0 for grpc, v3.0.5 for go-jose/v3,
# v5.9.2 for pgx, v0.311.3 for prometheus, v1.1.2 for buger/jsonparser) take precedence
# over the older versions listed in sub-module go.mod files. The compiled binary is safe.
# Reference: https://go.dev/ref/mod#workspaces

# go.opentelemetry.io/otel v1.37.0 in apps/*/go.mod and pkg/*/go.mod
# Root go.mod has v1.43.0 — workspace resolves to v1.43.0
CVE-2026-29181
CVE-2026-24051
CVE-2026-39883

# google.golang.org/grpc v1.74.2 in apps/*/go.mod and pkg/*/go.mod
# Root go.mod has v1.80.0 — workspace resolves to v1.80.0
CVE-2026-33186

# github.com/go-jose/go-jose/v3 v3.0.4 in apps/*/go.mod and pkg/*/go.mod
# Root go.mod has v3.0.5 — workspace resolves to v3.0.5
CVE-2026-34986

# github.com/jackc/pgx/v5 v5.7.5 in apps/*/go.mod
# Root go.mod has v5.9.2 — workspace resolves to v5.9.2
CVE-2026-33815
CVE-2026-33816

# github.com/prometheus/prometheus v0.303.1 in apps/*/go.mod or pkg/*/go.mod
# Root go.mod has a higher version — workspace resolves upward
CVE-2026-42151
CVE-2026-42154

# github.com/buger/jsonparser v1.1.1 in apps/*/go.mod or pkg/*/go.mod
# Root go.mod has v1.1.2 — workspace resolves to v1.1.2
CVE-2026-32285

# github.com/grafana/tempo (pseudo-version v1.5.1-*) — CVE-2026-21728, CVE-2026-28377
# The fix requires upgrading to github.com/grafana/tempo/v2 (major module path change).
# This is a CODE MIGRATION, not a simple bump: all import paths in pkg/tsdb/tempo/*.go
# must be changed from "github.com/grafana/tempo/..." to "github.com/grafana/tempo/v2/...".
# Additionally, both CVEs are in the Tempo SERVER (DoS via large queries, S3 key disclosure);
# Grafana uses tempo only as a CLIENT via protobuf bindings (pkg/tempopb) — the vulnerable
# server code paths are not in the execute path for Grafana.
# Tracked separately for a dedicated migration PR.
CVE-2026-21728
CVE-2026-28377

